<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap band__grid">
    <div class="rail">
      <p class="mono-label">The alliance seat</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Partnerships</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        An alliance only works when both companies can describe it the same way. That
        agreement doesn't happen on its own &mdash; someone has to sit between the two
        roadmaps and do the reconciling. That's the seat I work.
      </p>
      <p>
        At TrendAI I sit on the Global Alliances team across our hyperscaler partnerships,
        with the bulk of my time on AWS. I own the technical strategy for it: what we claim,
        how those claims hold up under engineering scrutiny, where our roadmap meets theirs,
        and what the executive story sounds like on each side of the table.
      </p>
      <p>
        The part people underrate is that an alliance is a practice, not a set of meetings.
        It needs enablement material, a repeatable technical story, and people who can carry
        it without you in the room. That's the part of this job I'd rather be measured on
        &mdash; and it's the thing I've ended up building at every company I've worked for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

